    text_method_arg_copied_through_extern_abi_per_call_2026-10-25, 1, "2026-11-10 lane work/p2-text-arg-extern-abi: premise re-checked, still valid. Root cause: ensure_tagged_str (src/compiler/50.mir/_MirLoweringExpr/method_calls_literals.spl) emitted rt_interp_cstr + rt_string_len + rt_string_new UNCONDITIONALLY for every text operand of a runtime text primitive, so an already-tagged receiver (file content) was copied per call (index_of per line = O(bytes x lines)). The lowering fix is already on release/1.0.0 via 74bf9d08fe0 (perf(mir): preserve proven tagged Text via raw bitcasts): the re-tag is guarded by a runtime raw-vs-tagged branch (blocks text_decode_nonnull / text_keep_tagged / text_box_raw / text_normalize_merge); a tagged handle passes through unchanged, only a raw char* is boxed. This lane adds the missing repro + prevention spec test/01_unit/compiler/50.mir/text_method_arg_extern_abi_no_copy_spec.spl (repro: two-arg index_of on a text param; per-line index_of loop. siblings: contains/find with a text-param arg, starts_with with an indexed [text] arg, nested needle.trim() arg, split with a text-param sep). It asserts the block that calls the primitive has no rt_string_new and that a text_box_raw block exists. Red on the pre-fix lowering (74bf9d08fe0~1: 0/7 passed, rt_string_new beside rt_text_find in the entry block) -> green on release/1.0.0 (7/7). Interpreter-only evidence; native verification = re-run the 1.17 MB / 20,000-line repro on a stage3 object (target RSS < 50 MB). The _driver_line_end byte_at workaround stays until then."

